<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan-Nov auto output up two pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan-Nov auto output up two pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia produced 792,000 automobiles in the first 11 months of this year, a rise of two percent on a year earlier, figures released by the State Statistics Committee on Sunday showed.</p>
<p>The committee released the following data:</p>
<p>  RUSSIAN VEHICLE OUTPUT	JAN-NOV 96 JAN-OCT 96 JAN-NOV 95</p>
<p>    Automobile total production   792,000    719,000</p>
<p>     yr/yr pct change			+2	   +2     +6</p>
<p>    Truck total production	  123,000    110,000</p>
<p>     yr/yr pct change		     -10	  -13    -20</p>
<p>    Bus total production	     34,700     31,800</p>
<p>     yr/yr pct change			-4	   -6    -16</p>
<p>					     NOV 96    OCT 96    NOV 95</p>
<p>    mth/mth pct change autos	  -18	  +22	-14</p>
<p>     yr/yr pct change		   +10	  +15	-20</p>
<p>    mth/mth pct change trucks	  +7	  +12	-13</p>
<p>     yr/yr pct change		   +28	   +7	-41</p>
<p>    mth/mth pct change buses	  -27	  +27	-30</p>
<p>     yr/yr pct change		   +18	  +16	-46</p>
<p>				Month/month</p>
<p>				 change by</p>
<p>				manufacturer</p>
<p>    GAZ			   -4</p>
<p>    UAZ			  -15</p>
<p>    AvtoVAZ		    -18</p>
<p>    Kamaz			+11</p>
<p>    ZiL			  +79</p>
<p>    Izhmash		    -30</p>
<p>    Moskvich(AZLK)	  closed</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
